@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Direct serial-peer endpoint
+
+`erbium_emu --uart-socket PATH` owns a filesystem AF_UNIX stream listener.
+Connect the Linux guest's UART1 (`ttyAMA1`) chardev to this path, separately
+from UART0's boot console and the framed `--api-socket` xSPI backend.
+Every byte received on this socket enters Shakti UART RX; every transmitted
+Shakti UART byte goes back to that same peer. No MMIO/console RPC, framing,
+terminal conversion, or emulator diagnostic text is inserted into this stream.
+
+This is the functional equivalent of host UART TX -> Erbium UART_RX (GPIO10)
+and host UART RX <- Erbium UART_TX (GPIO9), as described by the source RTL
+study in the enclosing project's `docs/uart-host-connectivity.md`.
+Firmware must still select `SystemConfig.uart_enable` (bit 6). This reliable,
+backpressured byte transport does not model baud timing, shift registers,
+electrical levels, framing errors, break, or physical RX overruns.
+
+## Ownership and reconnect policy
+
+* The pathname must not exist, including a stale socket. Nothing is removed
+  before bind. Inspect and manually remove a stale socket only after confirming
+  its previous owner is gone. A live listener, regular file, or symlink is never
+  displaced. Normal shutdown removes only the socket inode this instance bound.
+* One active full-duplex connection is retained. Additional connections are
+  accepted and immediately closed, not queued for later takeover. Admission
+  processing is bounded per emulator iteration.
+* EOF, half-close, hangup, or a socket error ends the session. The endpoint
+  detaches both borrowed UART fds and polls their FD interface **before** closing
+  the descriptor, then accepts a fresh connection. Bytes still in the closed
+  connection's kernel queues are discarded; bytes already in UART FIFOs remain
+  governed by the device. No unbounded reconnect spool/replay buffer is added.
+* CPU warm reset/POR does not recreate the listener or close a connected peer.
+  The normal device reset/pinmux rules still apply; a POR can disable the pads.
+  Whole-chip POR clears UART registers/FIFOs/interrupt state; CPU-only warm,
+  cold, and debug resets do not. Host bytes sent while pads are disabled are
+  discarded by the device's bounded RX service; reenable may also flush backlog.
+* No client means RX/TX attach to `-1`, not stdin/stdout. Device FIFO
+  backpressure governs queued TX; this is not a guarantee of lossless output
+  across unlimited disconnection or target FIFO-full writes.
+* SIGINT/SIGTERM allow normal cleanup even without an xSPI listener.
+  UART writes suppress their own SIGPIPE, without requiring the xSPI backend.
+* While CPU-held/WFI, the endpoint remains serviced. Idle waits are bounded
+  to 1ms when no simulation timer is running; a full RX FIFO does not cause a
+  readiness-driven busy loop.
+
+`--uart_rx_file PATH` and `--uart_tx_file PATH` (including existing single-dash
+spellings and PTY paths) remain available without `--uart-socket`. They cannot be
+combined with socket mode. UART and xSPI must use distinct socket pathnames.
+Attach the host/capture before releasing CPU reset to retain the boot banner.
+
+## Endpoint regressions
+
+From the enclosing repository root, build the isolated lifecycle test:
+
+```sh
+g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic \
+  -Iet-platform/sw-sysemu/sys_emu \
+  et-platform/sw-sysemu/sys_emu/uart_socket.cpp \
+  et-platform/sw-sysemu/tests/erbium/host/test_uart_socket.cpp \
+  -o /tmp/test_uart_socket
+/tmp/test_uart_socket
+```
+
+After the shared emulator build (`cmake --build build/sw-sysemu --target
+erbium_emu -j2`), run the independent backend integration regression:
+
+```sh
+python3 et-platform/sw-sysemu/tests/erbium/host/test_uart_endpoint.py \
+  --emu build/sw-sysemu/erbium_emu
+```
+
+These tests are endpoint/FD-lifecycle tests, not the UART register-fidelity
+suite and not the guest `erbctl load --start`/Kotama console acceptance test.
